<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11891"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 2:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Warrant issued in 20-year-old abuse case <BR>  <BR>AI from Collegeville:  <BR>  <BR>... a criminal statute of limitations doesn&#39;t begin to run until allegations are made to law enforcement, said Matthew Quinn, chief deputy in the Stearns County Attorney&#39;s Office.  <BR>  <BR>This is a good time to be reminded that there appears to be an even more dangerous predator at large targeting young males. In January 1989, a 12-year-old boy, JS, was kidnapped in Cold Spring, sexually assaulted, and -- thank God -- released. Later that year, on October 22, 1989, Jacob Wetterling was abducted near his home in St. Joseph, never to be seen again. Six months later, on April 20, 1990, 17-year-old Christopher Matthew Kerze disappeared while home sick from school in Eagan. His family&#39;s van was found abandoned two days later near Grand Rapids, MN, not very far from where Kevin Jay Ayotte was taken from his family&#39;s summer home in Sugarbush Township on September 30, 1982. Most recently, on November 10, 2002, St. John&#39;s University student Joshua Guimond disappeared while walking alone on campus.  <BR>  <BR>If you live in the St. Joseph-Cold Spring-Collegeville area, don&#39;t overlook anyone. Most sex offenders look just like us. They&#39;re the familiar stranger on your block. Jacob&#39;s abductor would now likely be 45-65 years of age. If you have any information or suspicions, no matter how insignificant you may think it is, please report it to the Stearns County Sheriff&#39;s Department at &#40;320&#41; 251-4240.  <BR>  <BR>Last year, the sheriff made a personal appeal to men who were boys aged 10 to 15 and living in or near St. Joseph or Cold Spring in the late 1980s and early 1990s to contact him if they were ever approached in a sexual manner by an adult man but never reported it to the police. By the same token, any past or present male college students in the area who have been approached in a sexual manner by an adult male and never reported it to the police, should immediately contact the sheriff at the above number.  <BR>  <BR>This could be the piece of the puzzle needed to solve the disappearances of Jacob Wetterling, St. John&#39;s University student Joshua Guimond, and several other young males that have gone missing in Minnesota since the disappearance of the Ayotte boy in 1982.  <BR>  <BR>Never give up hope. The BTK strangler in Wichita claimed his first victims in 1974 and was not arrested until last month -- 31 years later. He was the president of his church congregation and the compliance officer enforcing city codes in his community.  <BR>  <BR><a href="http://miva.sctimes.com/miva/cgi-bin/miva?Web/page.mv%2B1%2Blocal%2B584123%2B&amp;PageAction=Chat" target=_top>http://miva.sctimes.com/miva/cgi-bin/miva?Web/page .mv&#43;1&#43;local&#43;584123&#43;&amp;PageAction=Chat</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
