<!--Post: 12129--><!--Time: 1111615221-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12129"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 2:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Experts on serial killers praise Wichita authorities for handling of BTK case <BR> <BR>Matt Sedensky THE ASSOCIATED PRESS <BR> <BR> <BR>WICHITA, Kan. -- It took detectives 31 years to catch the man they believe is the BTK strangler, even though the killer scattered clues around and the suspect under arrest was not exactly hiding. But many experts on serial killers say the investigators deserve praise. <BR> <BR>Serial killers are notoriously hard to catch. <BR> <BR>&#34;The fact that the case wasn&#39;t solved for so long doesn&#39;t mean that they were going down the wrong routes,&#34; said James Alan Fox, a Northeastern University criminologist and author of the book &#34;Extreme Killing.&#34; &#34;If he wasn&#39;t so good at killing and covering his tracks and evading police, he would have been caught years ago.&#34; <BR> <BR>rest of article at website: <BR><a href="http://www.harktheherald.com/modules.php?op=modload&amp;name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=49155&amp;mode=thread&amp;order=0&amp;thold=0" target=_top>http://www.harktheherald.com/modules.php?op=modloa d&amp;name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=49155&amp;mode=thread&amp;ord er=0&amp;thold=0</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12129-->
<!--Post: 12130--><!--Time: 1111615960-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12130"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 2:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Unfortunately, there are no experts on serial killers.  <BR>If there were it wouldn&#39;t have taken 31 years to arrest BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
